      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to express \\(x^{2017}\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). Notice that this sum is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common ratio \\(r = x\\), and it has 2017 terms. The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}.\\]\n\nIn this case, the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is the sum of the first 2017 terms of the series with \\(a = 1\\) and \\(r = x\\):\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nFrom the given equation \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\), we can substitute this into the sum formula:\n\n\\[x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2,\\]\n\nprovided \\(x \\neq 1\\). Therefore, the value of the sum is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{2}.\\]",
